      "side": 1,
      "message": "aveCapabilitiesList() is now best-effort, it catches its own commit exceptions, logs, and keeps the device instead of failing the connection (matching netconf, where operational writes are fire-and-forget and \"device failed\" is session-driven, not write-driven). So the only failures reaching the handler are pre-registration, where the node was never in activeDevices.",
